Ideas taken, text not taken
---------------------------

The devil's advocate reviewer is an idea borrowed from the projects below.
None of their text appears in this repository; the prompt was written from
scratch for this roster and this schema. Two of the three carry no licence at
all, so copying from them would not have been permissible, and the fourth is
CC BY-NC, which would have forced this repository to be non-commercial.

  Imbad0202/academic-research-skills — https://github.com/Imbad0202/academic-research-skills
  CC BY-NC 4.0, Copyright (c) 2026 Cheng-I Wu
  Source of the devil's-advocate idea: a panel member whose remit is to argue
  against the paper rather than to look for a class of defect.

  nikhilklath/skills — https://github.com/nikhilklath/skills
  No licence stated. Its review-paper skill frames a pre-submission review as
  prioritised findings across contribution, identification, consistency, math,
  exhibits and prose. That framing informed how the devil's advocate is asked
  to rank what it finds.

  scunning1975/MixtapeTools — https://github.com/scunning1975/MixtapeTools
  No licence stated. Its Referee 2 persona is the source of the stance that a
  review is an audit that files a report against a checklist, rather than a
  reaction. Upstream already worked this way; the resemblance is noted because
  the idea was consulted.

  lcrawfurd/claude-skills — https://github.com/lcrawfurd/claude-skills
  No licence stated. Consulted for the same persona in a shorter form.


What this repository is not
---------------------------

It is not endorsed by, affiliated with, or reviewed by any of the projects
above. Defects in robusto are robusto's, not theirs. In particular, the
schema-contract layer that replaces provider-enforced structured output is new
here and is the most likely place for this port to behave differently from
upstream.
